      'The Green Revolution used high-yielding variety seeds with assured irrigation, fertilisers and pesticides. Its biggest success was in wheat, in irrigated regions such as Punjab, Haryana and western Uttar Pradesh. Pulses, coarse cereals and rain-fed regions gained much less, which increased regional inequality.',
