      'M. S. Swaminathan played the leading role in introducing and adapting high-yielding wheat varieties in India in the 1960s, working with Norman Borlaug\'s varieties. Verghese Kurien led the White Revolution (Operation Flood) in milk, while Raman and Bhabha were physicists.',
